.SH NAME
bprecvfile \- Bundle Protocol (BP) file reception utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBbprecvfile\fR \fIown_endpoint_ID\fR [\fImax_files\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBbprecvfile\fR is intended to serve as the counterpart to \fBbpsendfile\fR.  It
uses \fBbp_receive()\fR to receive bundles containing file content.  The content
of each bundle is simply written to a file named "testfileN" where N is
the total number of bundles received since the program began running.
.PP
If a \fImax_files\fR value of N (where N > 0) is provided, the program will
terminate automatically upon completing its Nth file reception.  Otherwise
it will run indefinitely; use ^C to terminate the program.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBbprecvfile\fR has terminated.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
The following diagnostics may be issued to the \fBion.log\fR log file:
.IP "Can't attach to BP." 4
.IX Item "Can't attach to BP."
\&\fBbpadmin\fR has not yet initialized BP operations.
.IP "Can't open own endpoint." 4
.IX Item "Can't open own endpoint."
Another BP application task currently has \fIown_endpoint_ID\fR open for
bundle origination and reception.  Try again after that task has terminated.
If no such task exists, it may have crashed while still holding the endpoint
open; the easiest workaround is to select a different source endpoint.
.IP "bprecvfile bundle reception failed." 4
.IX Item "bprecvfile bundle reception failed."
BP system error.  Check for earlier diagnostic messages describing the
cause of the error; correct problem and rerun.
.IP "bprecvfile: can't open test file" 4
.IX Item "bprecvfile: can't open test file"
File system error.  \fBbprecvfile\fR terminates.
.IP "bprecvfile: can't receive bundle content." 4
.IX Item "bprecvfile: can't receive bundle content."
BP system error.  Check for earlier diagnostic messages describing the
cause of the error; correct problem and rerun.
.IP "bprecvfile: can't write to test file" 4
.IX Item "bprecvfile: can't write to test file"
File system error.  \fBbprecvfile\fR terminates.
.IP "bprecvfile cannot continue." 4
.IX Item "bprecvfile cannot continue."
BP system error.  Check for earlier diagnostic messages describing the
cause of the error; correct problem and rerun.
.IP "bprecvfile: can't handle bundle delivery." 4
.IX Item "bprecvfile: can't handle bundle delivery."
BP system error.  Check for earlier diagnostic messages describing the
cause of the error; correct problem and rerun.
